{"issue": true, "summary": "In the `getParser` method, when a RegExp parser is matched, the code retrieves the parser using `parserRegExp.toString()` as the key, but the parser was stored with the actual RegExp object as the key in `customParsers`. This causes the lookup to fail and return undefined, leading to incorrect parser selection.", "edits": [{"path": "lib/content-type-parser.js", "old": "    if (parserRegExp.test(ct)) {
      parser = this.customParsers.get(parserRegExp.toString())
      this.cache.set(ct, parser)
      return parser
    }", "new": "    if (parserRegExp.test(ct)) {
      parser = this.customParsers.get(parserRegExp)
      this.cache.set(ct, parser)
      return parser
    }"}]}
